  "notes": "Sony BRAVIA KD-43X80L (2023, model string \"BRAVIA 4K VH22\", product BRAVIA_VH22_M_EU, device BRAVIA_VH22, MediaTek MT5895), EU\nAndroid 12 (Google TV, API 31), build BRAVIA_VH22_M_EU-user 12 STT2.230505.001.S136 682241 release-keys\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sony-kd-43x80l/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sony-kd-43x80l/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx (Google TV). Pass it to restore.sh as above.\nLive TV / tuner app: com.sony.dtv.tvx (set it as live_tv_package in the launcher's config.xml and hide it).\nKeep the com.sony.dtv.tvinput.* services, com.sony.dtv.braviasync*, com.sony.dtv.tvapi,\ncom.sony.dtv.sonysystemservice, settingsprovider, systemupdate/update (firmware), the Sony\nsettings apps and all com.mediatek.*: they drive HDMI, the tuner, Bravia Sync, updates and the remote.\nAlready disabled at the factory: com.sony.dtv.my5launcher, de.hdplus.tvapp.androidtv,\ncom.sony.dtv.soundslauncher, com.apple.atve.sony.appletv, com.sony.dtv.b2b.vendorprotocol,\ncom.youview.poa, com.sony.dtv.iplayerlauncher, com.sony.dtv.itvlauncher, com.sony.dtv.ardlauncher,\ncom.sony.dtv.b2b.softap, com.sony.dtv.all4launcher.\n\nTested and lived with on a KD-43X80L running the clean Apple TV style launcher (com.gathin.tvhome).\nsetupwraith disabled safely (Wi-Fi network owned by com.android.tv.settings, no reconnection issues).\nDisabling setupwraith gives Home back but can break casting (Chromecast built-in); comment out its line\nbelow if you want to keep casting.\nHDMI inputs (1-4, eARC), tuner TVX, remote control, and network streaming apps (Max, VLC, TIMVISION,\nRaiPlay) verified working across reboots.\nACR viewing tracker and telemetry",
